    "field": "Climate dynamics",
    "problem": "Most climate models fail to simulate the observed decadal variation patterns of the East Asian summer monsoon, leaving the responsible mechanisms\u2014whether internal climate variability or external forcings\u2014open to dispute and unresolved.",
    "method": "The authors apply ocean data assimilation to a coupled climate model, free of explicit GHG and aerosol forcings, to successfully simulate the decadal shifts of the East Asian summer monsoon by constraining the model with observed oceanic fields.",
    "task": "The task is to simulate the decadal shifts of the East Asian summer monsoon using a coupled climate model with ocean data assimilation but free of explicit greenhouse gas and aerosol forcings to determine if oceanic variations are the dominant factor for these transitions.",
