        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "extreme floods",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Northeast China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Later since the early 1990s, with the strengthening and northward shifts of the meridional wind, the anomalous wetter rain belt moves northward, leading to more extreme floods in Northeast China and a dryer Yangtze River in its middle and lower reaches4.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pacific Decadal Oscillation (PDO)",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "North China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Observational evidences showed that in the positive (negative) Pacific Decadal Oscillation (PDO) phase, with the warming (cooling) in the central and eastern tropical Pacific, summer precipitation in North China decreases (increases)8,9.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pacific Decadal Oscillation (PDO)",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "East China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Numerical experiments further demonstrated that the shift of PDO from positive to negative phase probably induces warming of the Lake Baikal and the weakening of the westerly jet through the air-sea interaction in the Pacific, changing the summer precipitation pattern in East China11,12.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Atlantic multi-decadal oscillation (AMO)",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "East Asia",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Meanwhile, others indicate that AMO can influence Mei-yu precipitation and tropospheric temperature of East Asia via a Eurasian wave train emanating from North Atlantic to China\u00b9\u2074.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "EI Ni\u00f1o-Southern Oscillation (ENSO)",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "East Asia",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Several factors are responsible for the decadal variation of EASM and the associated rainfall, including the decadal modulation of EI Ni\u00f1o-Southern Oscillation (ENSO)25, Tropical Indian Ocean warming26, PDO phase transition12, SST variation in the Atlantic26, etc.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "East Asia",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Any process that disturbs the normal monsoon rain belt would lead to relative drought or flood throughout East Asia, and affect the economy and society of the region\u00b3.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
